1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,190
I know the world moves fast.

2
00:00:02,190 --> 00:00:05,511
So you probably missed a huge AI breakthrough last week!

3
00:00:05,761 --> 00:00:08,873
A mathematician at Anthropic, working with Claude, released a

4
00:00:08,873 --> 00:00:10,529
proof of the Riemann hypothesis!

5
00:00:11,129 --> 00:00:14,241
Riemann found special numbers that encode the primes, and

6
00:00:14,241 --> 00:00:16,923
predicted all the important ones sit on one line.

7
00:00:17,173 --> 00:00:19,841
Earlier work showed at least two thirds of a

8
00:00:19,841 --> 00:00:20,968
key set follow it.

9
00:00:20,968 --> 00:00:22,154
But most isn't all:

10
00:00:22,154 --> 00:00:23,873
one exception would sink it.

11
00:00:24,123 --> 00:00:26,051
A proof says every single one does.

12
00:00:26,651 --> 00:00:27,600
And the proof?

13
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,689
17 million lines of code!

14
00:00:29,689 --> 00:00:31,904
Far too long for a person to read.

15
00:00:31,904 --> 00:00:33,802
So how do we know it's right?

16
00:00:34,052 --> 00:00:34,960
Two key checks.

17
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:36,833
First: is it the right question?

18
00:00:36,833 --> 00:00:40,863
Two separate tools confirmed it proves exactly the standard statement.

19
00:00:41,113 --> 00:00:42,594
Second: is every step right?

20
00:00:42,594 --> 00:00:45,300
It's written in Lean, a proof language whose checker

21
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,628
checks every single step.

22
00:00:46,878 --> 00:00:49,263
Several checkers by different people said yes;

23
00:00:49,263 --> 00:00:51,546
two are even proved unable to accept a false

24
00:00:51,546 --> 00:00:54,438
one, even if Lean's logic had a flaw. Certified correct!

25
00:00:55,038 --> 00:00:55,987
What does it mean?

26
00:00:56,237 --> 00:00:57,972
Certified doesn't mean understood.

27
00:00:57,972 --> 00:00:59,805
The checkers say it's true, not why.

28
00:00:59,805 --> 00:01:02,729
One mathematician says that could take months... or years.

29
00:01:03,329 --> 00:01:04,745
That's the real change:

30
00:01:04,745 --> 00:01:07,342
checking and understanding have come apart.

31
00:01:07,342 --> 00:01:08,463
AI helped find it.

32
00:01:08,463 --> 00:01:09,703
Machines checked it.

33
00:01:09,703 --> 00:01:13,657
Mathematicians still have to understand it, to build on its ideas.

34
00:01:14,257 --> 00:01:15,286
So, what we learned:

35
00:01:15,286 --> 00:01:17,686
a proven checker on the right question tells you

36
00:01:17,686 --> 00:01:18,274
it's right.

37
00:01:18,274 --> 00:01:19,940
Only understanding tells you why.

38
00:01:20,190 --> 00:01:20,712
Want more?

39
00:01:20,712 --> 00:01:23,181
Subscribe, and comment what we should explain next.
